THOUGHT: Start by defining the `Stack` class with the required methods: `push`, `pop`, `peek`, and `size`.
ACTION: write_file
PATH: s1_stack.js
```javascript
class Stack {
  constructor() {
    this.items = [];
  }

  push(item) {
    this.items.push(item);
  }

  pop() {
    if (this.isEmpty()) {
      throw new Error("Stack is empty");
    }
    return this.items.pop();
  }

  peek() {
    if (this.isEmpty()) {
      throw new Error("Stack is empty");
    }
    return this.items[this.items.length - 1];
  }

  size() {
    return this.items.length;
  }

  isEmpty() {
    return this.items.length === 0;
  }
}

module.exports = Stack;
```

